Medicine for the sensitive Heart, awakened Heart, a broken Heart ~ for the warriors, Earth keepers, Land stewards, sensitive souls this Venus day 🌹🐚

For easing our Spirit & nervous systems. Heart Medicines for us all💕I keep hearing “tend to your Hearts.” Physical & emotional. In TCM Summer correlates with the Heart {tho, we are nearing late Summer now}

How have your Hearts been feeling? I think many {all?} are feeling tender, an understatement. 

We must care for our Hearts. Fall in love with Creation. Finding moments of softness & joy too. Not in spite of grief, but honouring grief, love, our limited time here🍓 

Our Hearts are a potent organ of perception. Our common language is heard through the Heart ~ communing w Flowers, Trees, Animal kin.

Some Plant Medicines for the Heart:
✣Hawthorn: Heart tonic. May decrease LDL & blood pressure (BP), increases blood flow to Heart. Helping us drop into our hearts, so that we may listen, hear, speak & FEEL from this harmonious place. Healing.
✣Motherwort: Cardiotonic. Rhythmic. Cardiac glycosides, ease moon time cramps + spasms, moves Blood/stagnation, increases blood to Heart, energetic protection. A hug from Mama Earth. Calms Heart palpitations & anxiety. {In Womb Wisdom & Transitions}
✣Wild Rose: Heart Medicine. Tannins strengthen vasculature. Healing matrilineal trauma & remembering gifts. Protection & Heart boundaries. Love.
✣Linden: ♥️ shaped leaves, antispasmodic, may ↓ BP, calms nervous system, soothes headache from emotional stress/nervous system tension. Remembering our path & connection to Creation. 
✣Reishi: Strengthens Heart/cardiac function, nourishes Heart & Spirit, supports cognitive function/memory, longevity tonic {in Fountain of Youth elixir + Elixir of Life}
✣Alibizia: “Happiness Tree,” lifts the spirit, calming, Star consciousness, helps w low mood/mild depression, analgesic (pain relief)
{as always, there’s SO much more to each Plant.  Including interactions. Research, seek guidance, dosage, preparation,etc}

Please take care of your Hearts, Fam. Take care of one another’s Hearts 💗🌹Let's hold one another, our more than human kin & ourselves gently🦌 {Heart Song & Elixir of Life back in!}

My TCM (Traditional Chinese Medicine) Treasure Chest 〰️〰️〰️〰️ 

will be working on my substack this weekend and will share some of the places I go to in Chinatown to gather medicine! I’ve never been a tea person but I’m becoming a tea person because tea is now my medicine! 💊 

@drinktheqi has a pretty cool special going on right now with jujubes and gojiberries added to orders!

HEALTHY HABITS: EP 2 WARMTH 🔥✨

☯️ in TCM (traditional chinese medicine), warmth = life force 🔥🔥 and helps support your spleen, stomach and digestive fire.

on the other hand, cold foods slow down digestion, weaken your spleen, and can lead to bloating, fatigue, water retention, poor circulation, and even menstrual cramps. since swapping out cold & raw foods for more warm foods, my cramps disappeared and my appetite became so much more regulated 🙌🏻

⚠️ doesn’t mean I’ve completely cut out salads, smoothies, fresh fruit, etc!! 🍎 I’m just smarter about it so that it isn’t sooo cold 🥶 when it hits my stomach, i.e. I have it while sipping a warm drink, chew it longer before swallowing, or have smoothies & fruit that aren’t super cold but have been left out at room temperature for a while!

you can also incorporate more heating foods like: ginger tea, spices in your food, and cooked vegetables and proteins.

