short lil history of herbalism + a love letter to planties 🌱 

Some of my fave herb brands that i incorporate daily are:

@superfeast out of Australia for all things feel good; it’s a brand by incredible, incredible founders and a deep well of knowledge behind their brand. like beyonddd

@elixhealing creates personalized TCM-based tinctures based on what your menstrual cycle is telling you

@wishgardenherbs has a long list of targeted blends for all sorts of aims

^All of these brands are linked in my bio w/codes, too

i started a blog in the first place (2012) largely bc of this. all i wanted was clear skin and an easy period. yeah i wanted to perform better as an athlete, but i was excelling at that in a way, so it was just icing.

i couldn’t figure out my skin. and my period.

this has led me down a meandering road of learning what it means to look at the whole body (including emotions, things i believed about myself, light environment - all of it).

sunlight. herbs (which come from sunlight). nutrients. exertion. rest. bliss + vibes. self belief. self peace. a sense of “no limits, no rules.” these are some of the ingredients i’ve found along the way that are crucial. and i’m still finding them, which is a fun time.

herbs have had a special place for me bc i feel defensive of them - haha. they have been largely ignored or pushed to the side from the mainstream, labeled as alternative. nah. they are absolute medicine. (Check out my next reel for more on that.

